 "reviewHtml": "<div><p>If Jeff Spicoli had a rich mom, she would be wearing A.L.C.’s spring 2027 collection. Designer Andrea Lieberman’s brand has always married New York’s rough-and-tumble attitude with California’s cool nonchalance. But A.L.C.’s latest offering reads as Lieberman’s sartorial love letter to the West Coast.</p><p>“I’ve always believed in very sporty shapes in really elevated fabrics,” Lieberman said in her Flatiron showroom. While this applied to pieces like the sleek white floor-length dress with a neckline reminiscent of a tennis dress, a cotton-nylon anorak, and a silk satin boatneck T-shirt, Lieberman is always at her best when she goes full throttle. The highlight was a pair of board shorts that were instantly promoted from beach-bum staple to elegant summer mainstay thanks to their luxe silk fabrication. In keeping with the elevated beachwear, a black shirt with yellow and white stripes that almost felt like terry cloth was actually made of an Italian bouclé yarn.</p><p>There was a certain element of impish joy that shone through in this collection. The color palette helped. Lieberman was drawn to a toothpaste-y mint green this season, which took the shape of a V-neck sweater paired with a rich burgundy leather skirt. Always a stylist, Lieberman added one last jolt of electricity with a sneaky peek at a lace-trimmed tank top beneath the sweater. Still, nothing ever seemed overwrought. As Lieberman put it, “Everything should feel as easy as a T-shirt.”</p></div>",
